{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"bin/render must run with only PATH=/usr/bin:/bin from any working directory, locate the supplied helper and template, and write the requested output while retaining report contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests from a generated /tmp directory and, after restart, from / both succeeded under env -i with only the specified PATH. The generated output matched the supplied helper applied to the template and contained the complete report.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60dac472a06a4805","cmd-1b8d6b13eda2434f","cmd-3a5c8bd0b37e4ea1","cmd-3b19842b0c3f49b7"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the source template under /srv/legacy2/minimal-environment-job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The template retained its baseline SHA-256 hash before and after the repair and again after restart; its displayed contents also remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-1b8d6b13eda2434f","cmd-3a5c8bd0b37e4ea1","cmd-3b19842b0c3f49b7"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Alpine Linux 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were unchanged across execution and restart. The repair used a POSIX /bin/sh script and was directly executed successfully on that platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60d4a262799c4592","cmd-1b8d6b13eda2434f","cmd-3a5c8bd0b37e4ea1","cmd-3b19842b0c3f49b7","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"No unrelated or unnecessary system mutation was observed: replacing bin/render was the required repair, output generation supported bounded verification, and the reboot was required by the provider protocol. However, evidence artifacts were not cleaned up: cmd-3a5c8bd0b37e4ea1 left /tmp/render-verify.aMicaH and its two files, cmd-c9323ef92eb04a60 left /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, and cmd-3b19842b0c